{"resourceIdentifier":"4796","resourceName":"CACHOEIRA PORTEIRA CONSERVATION PROJECT","description":"The Cachoeira Porteira Conservation Project is located within the Brazilian Amazon, specifically in Oriximiná municipality in the Pará State, Brazil. The project zone, Cachoeira Porteira territory, has 225,289.53 hectares while the project area encompasses 178,450.77 hectares. Cachoeira Porteira, a remnant quilombo community, is represented by AMOCREQ-CPT, one of the project proponents. Systemica Inteligência em Sustentabilidade S.A is the other project proponent. The Cachoeira Porteira Conservation Project falls under the category of Improved Forest Management. The project activity is Logged to Protected Forest (LtPF), and it utilizes the VM0010 v.1.3 methodology. Therefore, the project shall reduce emissions and combat decreased carbon stocks by conserving the area that would be subject to planned timber harvest in the baseline scenario. The project´s crediting period is 30 years, commencing on November 7th, 2022, and it is expected to be concluded on November 6th, 2052. The estimated average net GHG emission reductions is 567,544.43 tCO2e per year, totaling 17,026,332.88 tCO2e, over the crediting period. It is noteworthy that the Cachoeira Porteira Conservation Project meets the gold level criteria for, climate, community, and biodiversity. In a comprehensive approach, seven activities have been meticulously planned, which are synergistic with the Sustainable Development Goals, including Zero Hunger, Good Health and Well-being, Quality Education, Clean Water and Sanitation, Affordable and Clean Energy, Decent Work and Economic Growth, Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure, Reduced Inequalities, and Life on Land.","location":{"latitude":-0.904718,"longitude":-57.026032},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2025-08-26","endExclusive":"2025-09-26","endInclusive":"2025-09-25"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type